{"arxiv_id": "2410.24029", "title": "Joint Training for Selective Prediction", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Jointly train the predictor and the abstention gate with a policy-gradient term (JTSP) and make the deferral head stake-aware — outputting a continuous stake fraction (0 = abstain) with the policy gradient on risk-adjusted units (Sharpe of weekly P&L) — since sports abstention is really a sizing decision, not a binary one.", "gate": "ADAPT accepted if JTSP beats the separate-gate Policy baseline by ≥ 2 points of posted-pick hit-rate at matched deferral rate on walk-forward seasons AND the JTSP-vs-JTSP-CE ablation shows the policy-gradient term (not just shared representations) contributes.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2411.00862v1", "title": "A Simple and Effective Temporal Grounding Pipeline for Basketball Broadcast Footage", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Add an event-driven scorebug-reading front end to the video lane: a change-detection layer that only OCRs frames where the scorebug region's frame-difference exceeds a threshold, then diffs consecutive reads into a discrete event stream (Q2, 3:42, 3rd&7) — cutting OCR compute ~10× and producing play boundaries directly instead of via timestamp matching.", "gate": "Adopt as the video lane's alignment stage if ≥90% of plays align within ±2 s of nflverse timestamps on held-out networks (a network not in training must be in the test set); reject if per-network retraining is required.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
