{"arxiv_id": "2505.22954v3", "title": "Darwin Gödel Machine: Open-Ended Evolution of Self-Improving Agents", "normalized_lane": "llm_agents_ai_scientist", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the open-ended self-improving signal-factory: an archive of candidate signals with staging screening (Stage-0/1 discards ideas before the expensive Stage-2 holdout), and make parent selection multi-objective — gate margin, novelty vs archive embedding, lineage productivity, plus a MAP-Elites diversity bonus over signal families (matchup, weather, rest, market-microstructure) to fill the thin lanes the curriculum wants to target.", "gate": "ADOPT the archive + staging if: arm (b) produces ≥2× the Stage-3-passing signals of arm (a) over 30 nights, ≥1 winner has a failed node in its lineage (stepping stones are real), and Stage-0/1 screening discards ≥70% of ideas before the expensive Stage-2 holdout.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INVENT", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2505.23437v2", "title": "Bounded-Abstention Pairwise Learning to Rank", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add a bounded-abstention pick-selection rule to the posting pipeline: select only picks whose confidence clears a conformalized conditional-risk threshold (Mondrian CP on edge-sign class) so risk estimates carry finite-sample coverage guarantees — replacing the paper's plug-in quantile threshold — and extend from pairwise to listwise (abstain on full slates, not pairs).", "gate": "ADOPT the rule into the posting pipeline only if, on the 2024–2025 test window, BALToR-selected picks beat the random-selection baseline by ≥1.5 pp hit rate at c=0.70 with empirical coverage within 0.02 of target, and beat the existing confidence-top-N rule (if any) by ≥0.5 pp. Otherwise REJECT.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2505.24783", "title": "Paired comparison models with strength-dependent ties and order effects", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt strength-dependent tie probabilities for GSE's soccer/NHL/boxing/push lanes — a Davidson-style tie parameter ν that rises with the average strength of the pair (β₁ > 0) rather than a constant ν — and test strength-dependent order (home-field) effects α₁ on NFL, including the HFA × quality interaction only if it improves ATS log-loss by ≥0.003 on 2018–2023 holdout, otherwise keeping flat HFA.", "gate": "Strength-dependent tie model must beat constant-ν Davidson by ≥ 0.005 out-of-sample 3-way log-loss on EPL 2022–2024 AND the β₁ coefficient must be positive with 95% CI excluding 0.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}

{"arxiv_id": "2506.00348", "title": "Beyond Winning: Margin of Victory Relative to Expectation Unlocks Accurate Skill Ratings", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace the ad-hoc tanh expected-margin curve with a market-informed one: E_MOV = spread-implied expected margin from the closing line, so the update's margin-surprise term becomes \"how much the result surprised the market\" rather than \"how much it surprised our own ratings\" — removing the circularity of ratings predicting margins that update ratings and connecting directly to the CLV lane.", "gate": "ADOPT the margin-surprise update into the team-strength layer if it clears the §12 gate on 2022–2025 NFL hold-out with no tuning after the gate is set. REJECT (do not merge) if it fails either metric, if the tanh fit is unstable across refits (parameter CV > 25%), or if it underperforms linear-MOV Elo.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.00613v1", "title": "WorldGym: World Model as An Environment for Policy Evaluation", "normalized_lane": "world_models_simulators", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the WorldGym-style harness for deployment decisions — a world-model environment for offline policy evaluation — replacing the single outcome head with a doubly robust estimator that combines the world-model rollout value with a model-free OPE estimator (weighted importance sampling on historical data) to correct the OOD-overestimation bias the authors flagged.", "gate": "ADOPT the harness for deployment decisions if: (a) Spearman ρ ≥ 0.7 between in-sim and real-backtest policy rankings on held-out 2024 (the paper's r=0.78 bar, rank version), AND (b) the harness identifies the best challenger variant using ≤50% of the real-game sample a pure backtest needs, AND (c) absolute value estimates track real backtest within the paper's reported band.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.01373v1", "title": "No Train Yet Gain: Towards Generic Multi-Object Tracking in Sports and Beyond", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt the McByte gating pattern for the video-tracking lane and fuse jersey-number OCR confidence as a third association cue alongside the mask: in ambiguity cases prefer the tracklet–detection pair whose OCR number matches the tracklet's majority-vote number — testing whether a football-specific identity cue beats the generic mask cue in same-uniform piles where masks are least reliable.", "gate": "ADOPT the McByte gating pattern if the McByte variant reduces ID switches by ≥ 30% vs ByteTrack on the 3-segment window with HOTA ≥ baseline; REJECT (keep ByteTrack/OC-SORT) if the gain is < 10% or throughput falls below 10 FPS offline-batch equivalent.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.02351v1", "title": "DIAMOND: An LLM-Driven Agent for Context-Aware Baseball Highlight Summarization", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Port DIAMOND to NFL as the automated first pass for weekly recap content and clip selection: replace the paper's hand-set scoring heuristics (1–60 bands, +1..+20 LLM adjustments, LI rank bonus) with a learned ranker trained on (play features, LLM narrative embedding) → human preference labels from GSE's own recap-selection history, optimizing pairwise ranking loss against broadcast ground truth.", "gate": "ADOPT as a GSE content tool if the NFL port beats WPA-only selection on F1 (≥5pp) and blinded narrative preference (≥60%) on the 20-game test; REJECT the LLM stages if no gain — ship the WPA+LI selector alone.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.03057v1", "title": "Partially Regularized Ordinal Regression to Adjust Teams' Scoring for Strength of Schedule and Complementary Unit Performance in American Football", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add punter/kicker-specific field-position value (expected post-punt/kickoff starting position given returner and coverage units) to the partially-regularized ordinal-regression scoring model's complementary feature set — testing whether return-game quality is a stable, predictive team trait that survives the elastic-net selection across seasons.", "gate": "Adopt complementary features permanently if 10-fold CV on 2015–2024 shows MAE improvement with SE bars non-overlapping vs GS+SoS in ≥4 of 10 seasons; otherwise keep SoS-only.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.03335v1", "title": "SportMamba Multi-Object Tracking", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt SportMamba's association design with jersey-number-conditioned association: replace the generic Re-ID embedding with a two-stream identity (a) a jersey-number OCR head producing a number posterior per detection and (b) team-side classification via jersey color clustering per game — association cost becomes a weighted sum of HA-EIoU, number-posterior agreement, and team agreement, attacking the paper's stated failure mode of near-identical uniforms.", "gate": "ADOPT the association design for GSE's video-tracking lane only if: on the football annotation set, the SportMamba-style pipeline beats ByteTrack by ≥ 3.0 HOTA points with the same detector, and the gain concentrates on occlusion-heavy plays.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.04282v1", "title": "DrSR: LLM based Scientific Equation Discovery with Dual Reasoning from Data and Experience", "normalized_lane": "symreg_equation_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add the DrSR dual-reasoning loop (insight extraction π_data + idea generation from experience) to GSE-SR and run an analyst-in-the-loop insight audit: present π_data's structured insights to a human analyst weekly as \"what the machine thinks it's learning about football,\" turning the module into a discovery communication channel whose insights (e.g., \"pressure rate residuals spike in dome games\") may surface real football hypotheses even when the equations disappoint.", "gate": "ADOPT dual reasoning if full DrSR-style beats plain GSE-SR by ≥15% OOD NMSE on 2024–2025 AND valid-program rate ≥90% (vs whatever plain achieves); REJECT if the insight/idea modules add cost without ≥15% gain.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.05763v1", "title": "Where Is The Ball: 3D Ball Trajectory Estimation From 2D Monocular Tracking", "normalized_lane": "world_models_simulators", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace the ballistic-only simulation with a 6-DoF football flight model including angular velocity state (spiral rate, wobble) and Magnus coefficients fit from NFL Next Gen Stats kick data, adding spin as a latent variable the end-of-trajectory network must implicitly detect from 2D wobble signatures — testing whether explicit orientation dynamics beat the sphere-assumption sim-to-real transfer on tumbling punts while matching on stable kickoffs.", "gate": "ADOPT the architecture if, on held-out real NFL kick/punt sequences with 2D tracks from broadcast video: (a) landing-spot error ≤ 1.5 yards mean absolute error, AND (b) beats the fitted-physics baseline by ≥25% on landing error, AND (c) sim-trained weights transfer (no more than 2× error inflation from synthetic validation to real).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.07860v1", "title": "Egocentric Event-Based Vision for Ping Pong Ball Trajectory Prediction", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adapt the event-based ball trajectory predictor to football flight with a drag+EKF model plus a Magnus/lift term whose spin-axis parameter is estimated from the ball ellipse's rotation across frames — testing whether spin-aware prediction beats drag-only on punts (highest spin) vs kickoffs.", "gate": "PURSUE the football flight-model adaptation if the drag+EKF model beats the constant-velocity baseline by ≥ 2 m on landing-point RMSE over the 20-clip window; otherwise REJECT and treat ball-flight estimation as buy-not-build (NGS air-distance family).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.09287", "title": "A Bayesian analysis of home advantage in professional squash", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a hierarchical Bayesian home model with team-specific home deviations (instead of a constant home field) plus an attendance/capacity-utilization interaction — testing whether real home-effect heterogeneity exists across NFL teams and how much of it crowds explain.", "gate": "Gate (ADAPT→keep): hierarchical home model beats constant-home baseline by ≥ 0.004 log-loss on 2022–2024 holdout AND ≥3 teams show |home deviation| > 2× posterior SD (i.e., real heterogeneity exists). Otherwise REJECT (keep constant home field).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.11399v1", "title": "Time-Varying Home Field Advantage in Football: Learning from a Non-Stationary Causal Process", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace the engine's static home-field number with a DYNAMO-style non-stationary causal learner that tracks how home advantage drifts over time, feeding DYNAMO-predicted per-drive expected points into the calibration layer so home edge is a time-varying causal quantity rather than a constant.", "gate": "Adopt the method for GSE only if, on the NFL reproducibility test, DYNAMO-predicted per-drive xP achieves MSE at least 10% lower than the raw-xP baseline on held-out weeks (the paper's Arsenal 2021-22 improvement, ≈29%, sets the bar; below 10% the complexity is not worth the NFL pipeline cost).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.13687", "title": "Enforcing Tail Calibration When Training Probabilistic Forecast Models", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "GSE adds a tail-weighted CRPS term to the probabilistic training loss and a TMCB diagnostic to the weekly calibration report, fixing blowout-tail miscalibration without degrading already-calibrated components.", "gate": "ADOPT twCRPS training term if the fine-tune experiment improves TMCB skill >=30% at t=10 with CRPS skill change >=-1% on the holdout season; if TMCB penalty alone is needed, accept only with overall MCB degradation <=20%.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.15578", "title": "Statistical post-processing of operational dual-resolution wind-speed ensemble forecasts", "normalized_lane": "weather", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "GSE builds an EMOS post-processing layer for stadium wind: truncated-normal EMOS with affine links on ensemble mean/spread fit per stadium on trailing 60-day windows, feeding the predictive distribution into the conformal weather layer.", "gate": "ADOPT if local/semi-local EMOS beats raw by >=5% CRPSS on wind speed at 0-3d leads on the 2023-2024 holdout; REJECT if gain <5% and rely on the ANET2 wind flow instead.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.15881v3", "title": "T-SHRED: Symbolic Regression for Regularization and Model Discovery with Transformer Shallow Recurrent Decoders", "normalized_lane": "symreg_equation_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "GSE builds GameSHRED: a transformer encoder with SINDy-Attention heads over lag-8 weekly team 'sensor' vectors that reads out stable, human-readable ODEs of team-state dynamics while matching the neural forecaster's spread MAE.", "gate": "ADOPT if GameSHRED's spread MAE is within 0.5 points of the engine's neural forecaster on 2025 AND >=2 heads yield stable human-readable ODEs AND total model size <100 MB; REJECT if MAE trails by >1.0 point.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.16253", "title": "Optimal Online Bookmaking for Any Number of Outcomes", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "GSE builds an adversarial-exposure diagnostic using closed-form online-bookmaking loss bounds, separating realized pick losses that fall inside the minimax envelope (adversarial flow) from losses that breach it (model misspecification).", "gate": "ADAPT confirmed if the closed-form envelopes compute cleanly on GSE data and the diagnostic separates within-envelope from model-error losses on at least 80% of game-weeks; REJECT if the envelope is vacuous (>3x the realized range).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.22350", "title": "Personnel-adjustment for home run park effects in Major League Baseball", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "GSE separates stadium effects from roster quality with a personnel-adjusted GLMM on points/FG makes, producing Denver-altitude-style adjusted stadium factors for the totals model and kicker props.", "gate": "ADAPT the elsewhere-covariate method if OOS totals RMSE improves >=0.3 points over raw venue means and >=3 stadiums move >=5 rank places between raw and adjusted scoring-friendliness.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.22450v1", "title": "Arnoldi Singular Vector perturbations for machine learning weather prediction", "normalized_lane": "mixed", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "GSE generates probabilistic game-day weather from the Pangu Weather 24h model perturbed by Arnoldi singular vectors (K~16 members, zero-mean pairs), extracting a stadium ensemble distribution rather than a point forecast.", "gate": "ADAPT if ensemble spread shows positive spread-skill correlation on hold-out games and tail-wind detection beats the deterministic baseline on totals residuals; otherwise keep only deterministic Pangu.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.23424v1", "title": "PETSA: Parameter-Efficient Test-Time Adaptation for Time Series Forecasting", "normalized_lane": "continual_online_learning", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "GSE freezes the main win-prob model after preseason and updates only a tiny weekly overlay (64 per-team adjustment terms + 2-3 global calibration parameters) on the prior week's games with Huber-robust loss.", "gate": "ADOPT if on 2020-2025 walk-forward the overlay beats the frozen model on anytime Brier by >=0.002 with ECE neutral-or-better AND captures >=80% of the full-refit gain.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2507.00028v2", "title": "HiT-JEPA: A Hierarchical Self-supervised Trajectory Embedding Framework for Similarity Computation", "normalized_lane": "selfsupervised_tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "GSE encodes 10Hz NGS tracking plays into hierarchical self-supervised trajectory embeddings (per-player sequences pooled by permutation-invariant attention) as retrieval and feature inputs for the matchup model.", "gate": "ADOPT if EITHER top-1 same-play-concept retrieval accuracy >=40% on held-out weeks 13-18 2024 (vs <=15% random, >=10pp above raw-DTW) OR downstream log-loss improves >=0.002 vs the no-embedding baseline.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2507.00333v1", "title": "Scope Meets Screen: Lessons Learned in Designing Composite Visualizations for Marksmanship Training Across Skill Levels", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "GSE hardens its analytics-visual doctrine: every visual breakdown stays video-anchored (real footage base layer with analytics overlaid, never a detached chart), built in novice and expert versions per the two-version rule.", "gate": "Accept as evidence for visualization design guidance only (preference + perceived understanding, honestly caveated); gate any GSE build on the reproducible test — do not redesign without it.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2507.02827v2", "title": "USAD: End-to-End Human Activity Recognition via Diffusion Model with Spatiotemporal Attention", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "GSE ports statistics-guided diffusion augmentation for rare NFL events (broken-tackle runs, coverage busts): per-play kinematic stats condition a label-conditioned DDPM that generates class-balanced synthetic plays to pretrain the event classifier.", "gate": "Accept as evidence that statistics-guided diffusion augmentation + adaptive composite loss improves imbalanced time-series classification; port only the augmentation recipe and composite loss, skipping the network.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2507.02904v1", "title": "Enhancing Sports Strategy with Video Analytics and Data Mining: Assessing the effectiveness of Multimodal LLMs in tennis video analysis", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "GSE builds film-analysis content tooling as a hybrid CV-to-text-to-LLM pipeline: cheap per-frame detectors convert footage to compact text (trajectories, ball positions, formation labels) for LLM narration and tactical Q&A, never MLLM-first video.", "gate": "PURSUE only if structured-feature prompting beats raw-frame prompting by >=25pp on event-sequence edit score on the 50-play window AND matches a cheap heuristic baseline.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2507.02906v1", "title": "Enhancing Sports Strategy with Video Analytics and Data Mining: Automated Video-Based Analytics Framework for Tennis Doubles", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "GSE builds a 'Labelling Factory' for proprietary charting-equivalent labels from footage (pre-snap OL splits, DB technique, pressure-path geometry) on a forked CVAT with NFL label schema, prototyping features before buying.", "gate": "ADOPT if the transfer-learned CNN reaches macro AUC >=0.80 for personnel/formation classification on the held-out game AND annotation throughput is >=2x the unaided manual rate; otherwise keep buying charting.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2507.04929v1", "title": "ConBatch-BAL: Batch Bayesian Active Learning under Budget Constraints", "normalized_lane": "active_learning", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "GSE allocates its weekly charting/labeling budget with ConBatch-BAL: a dollar-capped acquisition rule that admits games by cost-per-slot and scores them with BADGE/BatchBALD, beating cost-blind top-k.", "gate": "ADOPT the better of the two rules iff it beats cost-blind top-k at equal weekly dollar budget by >=0.005 held-out log-loss on the 2024 season simulation AND does not collapse in any single week (no week >2x average per-dollar regret).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2507.05470", "title": "Temporal Conformal Prediction (TCP): A Distribution-Free Framework for Adaptive Risk Forecasting", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "GSE wraps game-total intervals in temporal conformal prediction: rolling quantile models with a windowed conformal threshold and a Robbins-Monro update on weekly coverage errors, keeping rolling coverage within 2pp of nominal.", "gate": "ADOPT the RM adaptive layer if it keeps rolling coverage within 2pp of nominal over the 2025 season with width <= static conformal; REJECT the shrink heuristic if it causes systematic under-coverage; require an ACI baseline.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2507.05994v1", "title": "Beating the Best Constant Rebalancing Portfolio in Long-Term Investment: A Generalization of the Kelly Criterion and Universal Learning Algorithm for Markets with Serial Dependence", "normalized_lane": "sizing", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "GSE allocates bankroll across concurrent picks with periodic Kelly-style allocation: partition bet history into k=7 day-of-week or situational buckets, each learning its own allocation via the k-PUP update tuned to that bucket's return profile.", "gate": "ADAPT if on walk-forward (k chosen on 2023, evaluated 2024-2025) the k-PUP bankroll multiple exceeds flat fractional-Kelly by >=10% with max drawdown no worse than 1.2x the baseline's.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2507.06122", "title": "A Bayesian circular mixed-effects model for explaining variability in directional movement in American football", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "GSE extracts a per-season 'shiftiness' feature for RBs/WRs from von Mises mixed-effects models of ball-carrier movement on tracking data, predicting next-season YAC and missed-tackle rate.", "gate": "ADOPT if adding the shiftiness feature improves out-of-sample prediction of next-season YAC/attempt or missed-tackle rate over the current RB/WR feature set by >=0.02 R^2 (or significant at alpha=0.05); REJECT if no stable year-over-year signal.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2507.08108v1", "title": "Mallows Model with Learned Distance Metrics: Sampling and Maximum Likelihood Estimation", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "GSE aggregates weekly NFL power rankings from ~15-20 public and market-implied sources with an L_alpha-Mallows model, learning the league's upset-profile parameter alpha as a first-class feature.", "gate": "Adopt L_alpha-Mallows if on the 2025 held-out season it beats both baselines by >=2pp on pairwise accuracy AND >=5pp on top-5 hit rate in at least 3 of 4 seasons rolling; REJECT if alpha estimates are unstable.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2507.08921v1", "title": "Are Betting Markets Better than Polling in Predicting Political Elections?", "normalized_lane": "mixed", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "GSE classifies line moves as steam vs noise with a BSTS local-level model on de-vigged market-implied probability series: high tau^2/sigma^2 ratio means informed persistent moves, low means public churn.", "gate": "ADAPT-accept iff informed-steam-flagged moves achieve mean CLV >=+1.5% (de-vigged) vs <=+0.3% for unflagged moves over the 2023-2024 test set with n>=200 flagged moves.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
