{"arxiv_id": "2604.17194v1", "title": "Forecast Sports Outcomes under Efficient Market Hypothesis", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Swap GSE's odds-to-probability normalization to parameter-free OO-EPC as the default converter (used in CLV computation and consensus feeds — market-calibration infrastructure, not the objective), and fit FL-GLM favorite-longshot bias β per market per book as a standing mispricing diagnostic that steers where Kelly sizing is most aggressive.", "gate": "Adopt OO-EPC as the default converter if it significantly beats multiplicative normalization on holdout log-loss for a majority of (market, book) pairs with no pair significantly worse.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2604.17577", "title": "1623 Exact Finite-Horizon Quantile Kelly for Repeated Multi-Outcome Events", "normalized_lane": "sizing", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Build a finite-slate optimizer for GSE's published weekly slate: enumerate count chambers for the joint multinomial over the week's games, solve each shadow-Kelly problem in closed form, select the chamber maximizing α-quantile wealth, and convert the winning wealth profile back to stakes.", "gate": "ADOPT for the slate optimizer if quantile-Kelly delivers ≥10% higher realized median final bankroll than half-Kelly on the 2025–2026 season replay with no worse 5th-percentile bankroll; otherwise REJECT.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2604.18210v1", "title": "TacticGen: Grounding Adaptable and Scalable Generation of Football Tactics", "normalized_lane": "world_models_simulators", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Train a drive-level diffusion transformer over play descriptors + personnel/formation embeddings, using classifier guidance toward betting objectives (e.g., TD drives, shootout scripts) to produce conditional game-script distributions for derivative pricing and scenario content ('paths to the over hitting').", "gate": "ADOPT classifier-guided drive generation for scenario/derivative pricing if guided hit rate ≥3x base rate on 2024 held-out drives AND sample entropy ≥70% of unconditional (no collapse).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2604.19340", "title": "Improvements to the post-processing of weather forecasts using machine learning and feature selection", "normalized_lane": "weather", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build weather/lgbm_postprocess.py: LightGBM post-processing of HRRR forecasts at all 30 NFL stadiums (11x11 surface + 7x7 pressure-level windows at kickoff lead times, FS0 tau=0.9, Optuna tuned) for temp/wind/precip, paired with the ANET2 probabilistic model as mean + uncertainty.", "gate": "ADOPT if LightGBM beats raw HRRR by ≥ 10% RMSE on wind speed AND ≥ 5% on temperature on the 2023 holdout (matching the paper's margin scale).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2604.20172v2", "title": "Cover Meets Robbins While Betting on Bounded Data: ln n Regret and Almost Sure ln ln n Regret", "normalized_lane": "uncertainty_decision_theory", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Layer a 50-50 Cover-Robbins mixture as the global weekly stake multiplier on top of per-pick Kelly fractions, with anytime-valid edge-monitor gates: scale stakes 1.5x when test wealth W_n >= 20 (rejecting no-edge at alpha=0.05) and halve stakes plus trigger model review when W_n <= 0.5 after >=50 picks.", "gate": "ACCEPT if chronological backtest: realized regret R_n ≤ 2x the paper's theoretical bound constant at n = full sample AND final log-wealth ≥ 0.9 x oracle constant-fraction AND the shuffle test keeps W_n < 20 in ≥95% of shuffles (Ville validity holds on sports data).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2604.21087", "title": "Model Quality in Football: Quantifying the Quality of an Expected Threat Model", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt the bootstrap error-quantification protocol for GSE's possession-value / expected-points surfaces: simulate from the fitted model (>=500 replications), fit log(error) = c + alpha log K + beta log n, and only publish player ratings or prop prices from the surface if P(error < threshold) >= 0.90; otherwise coarsen the grid.", "gate": "Replicate on StatsBomb open data: require fitted α ∈ [0.9, 1.1], β ∈ [−1.15, −0.9], R² ≥ 0.8; then apply to one GSE EPV surface and confirm the 0.0192-style threshold (rescaled) gates at least one currently-used grid as invalid.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2604.24366v2", "title": "The Anatomy of a Decentralized Prediction Market: Microstructure Evidence from the Polymarket Order Book", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Port the CLOB-to-on-chain join pipeline to replicate the eight stylized facts on NFL/CFB Polymarket markets; build a longshot spread-premium curve by sport to downweight wide-spread market prices in GSE's signal fusion; adopt the wash-share lower-bound detector as a market-quality filter before trusting any venue's volume figures.", "gate": "Adopt the sports-only replication and the spread-premium signal-weighting if direction-agreement and stylized facts replicate within sampling noise.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2604.24517v2", "title": "Prior-Agnostic Robust Forecast Aggregation", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace the current ensemble combiner with the dampened log-odds pair combiner f_alpha (alpha=0.585) on the two strongest engine components, or the marginal-corrected variant with mu = de-vigged market consensus (alpha=0.656089, gamma=0.498268); backtest walk-forward on picks 2025 vs the current combiner and vs simple average.", "gate": "ADOPT the dampened log-odds pair combiner if it beats the simple (α=1) average by ≥0.002 Brier on 2025 walk-forward (DM p<0.05) with no log-loss regression; separately ADOPT the marginal-corrected variant if it additionally beats the plain α=0.585 rule by ≥0.001 Brier.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2604.24723v2", "title": "Efficient Multivariate Kelly Optimization Reveals Sigmoidal Scaling Laws", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace per-pick fractional Kelly on weekly slates with the O(TN) multivariate Kelly Newton-CG solver (joint log-growth maximization over up to ~10 simultaneous picks), and measure how far the independence-assuming solver over-bets on same-game correlated slates to calibrate a correlation guard.", "gate": "At N = 10 over 100 random instances: max relative error vs brute force ≤ 10⁻⁶; Newton-CG optimum ≥ greedy lower bound on every instance; adopt as the slate stake allocator if it beats current per-pick fractional Kelly on realized log-wealth and max drawdown on Neon picks slates.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2604.25280v1", "title": "The optimal betting wealth growth rate", "normalized_lane": "mixed", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace the arbitrary 0.25/0.5 fractional-Kelly multiplier with a principled uncertainty-haircut multiplier derived from the KL gap between the engine's edge D(p-hat||q) and the inf-KL over the uncertainty class (p-hat +/- calibration error bars), sizing in weekly slate blocks rather than per game.", "gate": "ADOPT the uncertainty-haircut fraction if, on 2024, it achieves ≥90% of full Kelly's log-growth with ≤70% of its maximum drawdown.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2604.27041", "title": "The Signal Credibility Index for Prediction Markets: A Microstructure-Grounded Diagnostic with Weighted and Time-Varying Extensions", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Port the Signal Credibility Index to line moves as informed-flow surveillance: score each >=1.5-point spread move with PR (price reversion on logit-transformed implied probs), TS (cross-book direction), and cross-book breadth HHI (a move led by Pinnacle/Circa alone = concentrated/informed), re-weighted for information content; use high-SCI_info moves to upweight GSE's own numbers.", "gate": "Adapt the SCI framework (both flavors) into GSE's steam pipeline if: (i) fitted NFL weights on ≥300 labeled moves achieve AUC ≥ 0.70 for move-side cover prediction; and (ii) the information-content and coordination-credibility flavors rank moves differently (Spearman < 0.6).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2604.27865v1", "title": "KellyBench: A Benchmark for Long-Horizon Sequential Decision Making", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Build GSEBench: a KellyBench-style walk-forward season simulator (weekly slate -> engine probabilities -> fractional-Kelly staking -> settle -> log-wealth) with progressive data disclosure, plus a staking-contract unit test proving the bet-time sizing function equals the specified Kelly function on 100% of placed bets.", "gate": "Adopt the GSEBench harness + staking contract if, across the 2022–2024 walk-forward sims: (a) fractional-Kelly staking beats flat staking on final log-wealth in ≥ 2 of 3 seasons with no ruin in any season; (b) the walk-forward-retrained engine beats the static engine on R in ≥ 2 of 3 seasons; (c) the integration test proves the invoked sizing function equals the specified Kelly function on 100% of placed bets.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2605.00459", "title": "Information Leakage at Population Scale: An Evaluation of the Polymarket Insider-Relevant Subpopulation, 2020–2026", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Build an NFL ILS analog ('pre-close drift share'): compute each game-week's line movement share before vs. after public anchors (injury report release, inactive list) with a hazard-decay correction for natural drift toward close, and feed anchor-robust early-drift scores into GSE's informed-flow suite.", "gate": "Adapt the ILS framework into GSE's steam/informed-flow suite if: (i) the anchor-robust subset shows a drift-share/cover correlation significant at p < 0.05 on 2024–2025 NFL; and (ii) the anchor-robustness gate filters out ≥50% of raw flagged games.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2605.00864", "title": "Arbitrage Analysis in Polymarket NBA Markets", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Run a standing Polymarket NFL arb monitor at ~4s top-of-book cadence: flag single-market (Ask_Yes + Ask_No < 1.00) and combinatorial (ML-vs-spread synthetic-short) dislocations with mirrored-liquidity dedup, producing a nightly 'market sharpness' efficiency digest that GSE's own probabilities are measured against.", "gate": "Adopt the monitor as a standing benchmark if, on 4 weeks of 2026 NFL Polymarket data, it detects ≥1 genuine in-game dislocation with measured executable depth while keeping post-game false-positive rate at 0.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2605.02287", "title": "Per-Market Information Leakage and Order-Flow Skill: Two Methodological Lenses on Informed Trading in Decentralized Prediction Markets", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Build a skilled-flow watchlist on Polymarket NFL markets: replicate the 10,000-draw sign-randomization test to identify skilled accounts, compute per-market pre-kickoff front-loading (ILS), and weight GSE's line-move signals by whether they originate from watchlist accounts.", "gate": "ADAPT is confirmed if, on 2024 Polymarket NFL data, the sports-only replication achieves ≥35% out-of-sample retention of the skilled-winner label AND high-ILS markets show ≥4pp better move→outcome prediction than unflagged markets.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2605.02611", "title": "Selective Prediction from Agreement: A Lipschitz-Consistent Version Space Approach", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace the empirical-disagreement abstention rule with Lipschitz-forced selection heads (spectral-normalized, trained on oracle post/don't-post labels from graded picks): post only games in the forced set computed from the Lipschitz envelope over the slate's game embeddings, then tighten bounds with local per-region Lipschitz constants.", "gate": "ADAPT the forcing rule iff forced picks beat the empirical-disagreement baseline by ≥1 selective-ROI point at matched coverage on chronological slate evaluation.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2605.05487v1", "title": "Cross-individual generalizability of machine learning models for ball speed prediction in baseball pitching", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt leave-one-player-out as a mandatory validation gate for all GSE player-level prop models (report LOPO R2/MAE alongside pooled CV as the honest generalization estimate for new players), and add a signed-residual 'efficiency' metric for players systematically outperforming their statistical inputs.", "gate": "Adopt LOPO as a mandatory validation gate for all GSE player-level models if the pooled→LOPO MAE degradation is material (≥ 10% relative) on the 2023–2024 test.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2605.06822v1", "title": "SHARP: A Self-Evolving Human-Auditable Rubric Policy for Financial Trading Agents", "normalized_lane": "llm_agents_ai_scientist", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Deploy SHARP as GSE's production policy layer: transcribe current production logic into a bounded rubric (<=40 condition-action rules over engine features), and run a weekly attribution agent that maps the 20 worst betting days to rule IDs, proposes atomic edits with full audit trails (rule ID -> error days -> validation score), and checks rule-interaction effects before accepting any edit.", "gate": "ADOPT if: evolved rubric beats Static by ≥3pp ROI (or ΔBrier ≥ 0.002) on the 2025 walk-forward, the A2 free-form arm underperforms Static, max drawdown does not worsen vs Static, and every rule edit has a complete audit trail.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INVENT", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2605.09599", "title": "Adaptive Liquidity in Prediction Markets via Online Learning", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Compute the hybrid signal Gamma^hyb (slippage-analog + liability-analog) weekly on GSE's pick/stake log as a state-dependent exposure framework: scale slate stakes inversely with the liability component so GSE's exposure adapts to correlated-slate risk, with the mixture construction's (1/beta)log M overhead guarantee bounding the cost of adaptivity.", "gate": "Adapt the mixture construction and the hybrid signal as GSE's state-dependent exposure framework if the liability component correlates with realized drawdowns on GSE's log.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2605.10717v1", "title": "Heteroscedastic Diffusion for Multi-Agent Trajectory Modeling", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add heteroscedastic uncertainty to GSE's trajectory forecaster: attach the L_NLL head (lambda=0.01, stop-grad on mean) with diagonal-Jacobian reverse Gaussian sampling onto the existing diffusion model, and train RankNN (K=20 modes, differentiable Spearman vs SADE) to e-rank modes — the Top-1 mode plus calibrated per-state ellipses give the pick and the position size.", "gate": "ADOPT the U2Diffine/RankNN delta if ALL of the following hold on the held-out test: (i) AccRate@95% ≥ 90% on football tracking; (ii) median Spearman ρ between e and SADE ≥ 0.50; (iii) e-ranked Top-1 minSADE20 beats random Top-1 by ≥8%; (iv) U2Diff sampling cost ≤ 20ms/mode at K=20.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2605.14855v1", "title": "Exploitation of Hidden Context in Dynamic Movement Forecasting: A Neural Network Journey from Recurrent to Graph Neural Networks and General Purpose Transformers", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt the CNN-LSTM context architecture (kernel adapted to football's frame rate; static landmarks = goal line, end zones, first-down line) for ball-carrier + nearest-defender 2s trajectory forecasting from NGS tracking, sweeping input lengths 0.5-4.0s.", "gate": "ADOPT the CNN-LSTM context architecture if, on the held-out weeks 15–18 test set, it beats the constant-velocity baseline by ≥15% FDE AND beats the plain 2-layer LSTM by ≥5% FDE at the 2.0s horizon.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2605.16066v1", "title": "A Market-Calibrated Accelerated Failure Time Model for In-Play Football Forecasting", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Calibrate GSE NFL team strengths per game to kickoff consensus lines (The Odds API consensus): minimize the sum of squared gaps between market-implied and engine probs over spread/moneyline/total implied probs, with the totals market fixing the absolute scoring level (identifiability fix), and report the calibration-shift distribution per team as an engine-honesty diagnostic.", "gate": "Accept into the engine lane if: (1) the kickoff-calibration objective is implemented and its identifiability fix (totals-equivalent market) documented; (2) held-out accuracy/RPS/log-loss reported against market-implied probabilities; (3) any profitability claim passes the goal-window-style timing control.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2605.20134v1", "title": "TrajTok: Adaptive Spatial Tokenization for Trajectory Representation Learning", "normalized_lane": "selfsupervised_tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build adaptive H3 spatial tokenization from 7 seasons of player positions (vocab 1.5-3k cells, fine near LOS, coarse deep), train the factorized encoder with co-masked objective (mask ratio 0.30) + ST-RoPE, freeze it, and attach adapters for play-similarity retrieval, route-family classification, and ball-carrier yards-gained regression.", "gate": "ADOPT if: (a) adaptive-tokenizer retrieval MRR ≥ 15% above fixed-resolution baseline on held-out weeks, AND (b) frozen-encoder route classification macro-F1 ≥ 0.60.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2605.23854v1", "title": "Entrywise Error Bounds for Spectral Ranking with Semi-Random Adversaries", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add MMWU-reweighted rank centrality as a GSE power-rating component: run the SDP/greedy edge reweighting maximizing the spectral gap on the season's comparison graph (downweights intra-division echo-chamber games, upweights inter-conference games), and publish 1/lambda_{n-1}(L^W) as a spectral-gap confidence diagnostic on every rating.", "gate": "Adopt reweighted spectral ratings as a GSE model component if MMWU-reweighted rank centrality beats unweighted on end-of-season l_infty error (vs batch-BTL) in ≥ 5 of 7 test seasons AND on next-week SU log-loss by ≥ 0.001/game averaged over 2018–2024.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2605.24445v1", "title": "Matrix Concentration Inequalities for Time-Inhomogeneous Markov Chains", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace fixed-K Elo updates with a drift-calibrated step eta = c*sqrt(Delta-hat), where Delta-hat is per-week skill drift estimated from batch-BTL weekly fits (c tuned on 2021-2022), and publish trailing-averaged ratings with the Theorem-29-certified window T instead of point-in-time ratings.", "gate": "Adopt drift-calibrated η for GSE's online ratings if it beats fixed-K Elo on next-week SU log-loss by ≥ 0.002/game averaged over 2020–2024 AND the optimal tuned c is stable across the tuning and test windows.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2605.28816v1", "title": "Gamma-World: Generative Multi-Agent World Modeling Beyond Two Players", "normalized_lane": "world_models_simulators", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build an NFL play-transition world model: 23 tokens (22 players + ball) per timestep with Simplex Rotary Agent Encoding (pool V=32, no learned player-slot embeddings so trades/call-ups need no retraining), Sparse Hub Attention with K=8 hubs, flow-matching training on NGS tracking transitions; then dedicate hub slots to ball state, down/distance/clock, formation, and defensive shell as semantically structured hubs.", "gate": "ADOPT if on held-out 2024 plays: (a) +1s mean entity position error ≤ 1.2 yards, AND (b) permutation-invariance holds (shuffled entity order changes error <2%), AND (c) SHA attention FLOPs ≤40% of dense at 23 entities with no error regression.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2605.29395v2", "title": "Low Rank for Rank: Uncertainty-Aware Task-Specific LLM Ranking under Sparse Pairwise Comparisons", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Fit a low-rank context-specific team-strength matrix (rows = game-context clusters from spread/total/rest/dome/divisional, columns = 32 teams; nuclear-norm + refinement BTL on outcomes) for early-season sparse contexts, and run three-way pick certification (certified vs unresolved) on the weekly published sheet.", "gate": "Adopt the low-rank context-rating estimator if it beats per-context BTL on next-season SU log-loss by ≥ 0.003/game averaged over the 2023–2024 test seasons AND produces strictly narrower mean rank CIs at ≥ nominal coverage on a 2024 holdout.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2605.30209v1", "title": "Betting Against Integrity: Identifying Match-Fixing Through In-Play Market Dynamics", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Fit a hurdle-ARX(1) state-space model on public NFL live odds (The Odds API in-game, 1-minute resolution; covariates: pre-game implied probs, score diff, time remaining, timeouts, events); use standardized residuals vs expected activity as a live-betting edge signal — flagged cells that cluster before line moves the pre-game model missed become GSE's steam/stale-line detector.", "gate": "ADAPT conditional on §12: fit the baseline hurdle SSM on one season of live odds-movement data; require ΔAIC ≥ 10⁴ over the no-state hurdle before proceeding; adopt only if flagged residuals predict line moves above chance.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2605.31529v2", "title": "SVI-Bench: A Dynamic Microworld for Strategic Video Intelligence", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Replicate the SVI data-engine pattern for NFL: game-clock alignment of broadcast clips to nflverse play-by-play, cross-modal entity resolution into per-game identity graphs, LLM-assisted QA/forecast instance generation, three-stage QC; adopt the T5 multiple-choice outcome-forecasting eval protocol (fixed observation windows, target events beyond the window) for GSE's forecasting models.", "gate": "ADAPT the data-engine pattern and T5 eval protocol if: the NFL pilot corpus (10 games) achieves ≥ 95% auto-consistency of generated instances against play-by-play logs, and the T5-style eval reproduces the paper's qualitative pattern (accuracy degrading with horizon, CE measurable and improvable with finetuning).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.02547v1", "title": "Pluralistic Leaderboards", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Run a weekly stability audit on GSE's published pick sheet: cluster games into matchup-context clusters, define cluster preference as realized pick profitability within cluster, compute gamma-hat per weekly top-k prefix; if excluded picks are systematically preferred by cohesive game-type subgroups, restructure the sheet with checkpoint-blockwise stable construction.", "gate": "Adopt the stability audit as a standing weekly check if the backtest finds γ̂ > 1 violations in ≥ 15% of weeks at any k ≤ 5 (2022–2024).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.02663", "title": "AdaWeather: Adaptively Mixing Probabilistic Weather Forecasts with Logarithmic Regret", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add a hybrid forecast combiner for GSE's sub-model predictive distributions (spread/total/win-prob): offline gradient-boosted combiner trained on 2020-2023 forecasts-to-outcomes plus an online exponentially-weighted CRPS mixture over sub-models + the offline combiner, updated weekly with strictly causal updates.", "gate": "ADOPT if the hybrid beats both the offline-only and online-only ablations on CRPS (≥2% each) and its cumulative regret vs. the season BIH stays within the logarithmic envelope (no linear-regret regime).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.03805v1", "title": "Regularization in Paired Comparison Models via Pseudo-Games and Phantom Players", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Regularize GSE's weekly in-season BT power ratings with phantom players: fit weekly BT on nflverse with a zero-strength phantom opponent and rho tuned by leave-one-week-out CV, so one early blowout cannot create an extreme rating while average teams stay untouched.", "gate": "Adopt phantom-player regularization for GSE's weekly in-season ratings if it beats ordinary BT on remaining-season log-loss in ≥ 17 of 24 test windows (weeks 1–8 × 2022–2024) AND beats or ties ridge BT on the same windows.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.04387v1", "title": "Rethinking Sales Lead Scoring with LLM-based Hierarchical Preference Ranking", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Weight GSE's team-rating BT fits by game informativeness via tiered-margin BT: fit P(i beats j | m) = sigma(theta_i - theta_j - m) with margins m=1.0 for playoff games, 0.5 for late-season contender games, 0.1 for early-season games, so ratings separate more on high-information games; then learn the tier margins end-to-end constrained non-increasing.", "gate": "Adopt if the tiered-margin BT beats static BT on next-season SU log-loss by ≥ 0.005 per game (averaged over the 2022–2024 rolling test seasons) AND the margin ablation shows tiered ≻ uniform ≻ none.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.04900v1", "title": "Multi-objective probabilistic forecast combination for inventory demand", "normalized_lane": "mixed", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Choose GSE's model-zoo combination weights with NSGA-III over (log-loss on outcomes, Kelly-simulated bankroll growth) on a rolling validation season and deploy the Pareto-knee weight vector — optimizing the actual betting objective rather than pure accuracy.", "gate": "ADOPT the knee-weight combination if, on the 2024 test season, it achieves bankroll ROI ≥ the log-loss-optimal weights' ROI while its log-loss is within 2% of the log-loss-optimal.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.05332v1", "title": "GITCO: Gated Inference-Time Context Optimization in TSFMs", "normalized_lane": "timeseries_foundation", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Wrap GSE's frozen sports TSFM in a Gate->Router->Critic->SMA serving module: train the gate on leave-one-game-out influence labels (did removing game X improve the forecast?), add a regime-shift detector probe (coaching/QB change) that forces gate abstention so genuine regime changes are never smoothed, and default to abstention since gate precision > recall is the safe direction.", "gate": "ADOPT as a default-on serving wrapper if the sports gate achieves ≥70% precision on 2022–2024 AND mean MASE reduction ≥1.5% with no season worse than baseline; keep it default-off if precision is 60–70%; REJECT if precision <60% or any season degrades.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.05551v2", "title": "Conformal Risk-Averse Decision Making with Action Conditional Guarantee", "normalized_lane": "uncertainty_decision_theory", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add an action-conditional conformal bet/no-bet filter (alpha=0.05, utility = realized profit) over the engine's calibrated outcome distributions on a rolling 4-week calibration set, publishing the guaranteed profit floor certificate nu(x) conditioned on betting; extend to utility-conditional stake tiers (0, 0.25f*, 0.5f*, f*) so the max-min rule selects the largest stake whose worst-case certified utility is positive.", "gate": "ACCEPT if ALL hold on the 3-season backtest: (1) empirical action-conditional coverage ≥95% where AC-RAC selects 'bet'; (2) Sharpe_AC-RAC ≥ 1.10 x Sharpe_baseline AND Calmar_AC-RAC ≥ 1.10 x Calmar_baseline; (3) bet volume ≥ 30% of baseline volume.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.07433v1", "title": "Watch, Remember, Reason: Human-View Video Understanding with MLLMs", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Structure GSE's broadcast-video pipeline as watch->remember->reason: watch = the tracking stack (detections, tracks, play grounding), remember = a play-structured game memory keyed on play boundaries with evidence pointers to timestamps, reason = query-driven evidence retrieval returning timestamp/box-grounded answers (e.g., 'every 3rd-and-long blitz in Q3' returns clips + boxes, not text).", "gate": "ADAPT the architecture (watch–remember–reason with budgeted evidence search) for GSE's video lane if: the primary read-throughs (DeepSport, FineQuest) replicate their core claims on inspection, and a prototype reasoner on the NFL query set beats uniform-sampling VLM QA by ≥ 15 points of answer accuracy with evidence IoU ≥ 0.5.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.07492v1", "title": "Bradley-Terry Rankings for Recommender Systems Across Dataset Taxonomies", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build regime-conditional team strength via fusion-regularized covariate BT: weekly win matrices over recent seasons with covariates (home/away, rest differential, dome/outdoor, wind bucket, QB-missing flags) fit by L-BFGS-B to get beta_{i0} + <x, beta_i>, usable as a regime-sliced margin-model feature; adopt the transitive-triplet ratio of weekly implied rankings as a standing model-selection metric.", "gate": "Adopt the covariate-BT component if, on the 2022–2024 rolling test seasons, it beats the static-BT baseline by ≥ 0.01 log-loss per game AND achieves a higher transitive-triplet ratio on weekly implied rankings, with no worse top-3 overlap.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.07811", "title": "When Do Markets Fully Process Public Information? Evidence from Real-Time Prediction Markets", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Build GSE's own out-of-sample in-play win-probability benchmark on nflverse play-by-play (cross-fit, no market input) and audit in-play market updating: estimate Delta p = alpha + beta Delta q to replicate the <1 updating finding on 2024-2025 NFL, then restrict drift-following to cross-book opportunities where a soft retail book lags a sharp book (Pinnacle) — executable because the stale price is taken, not the lagging book's spread.", "gate": "Adapt the updating-gap framework into GSE's in-play product if, on 2024–2025 NFL: (i) β is significantly below 1 and drift ρ significantly positive net of benchmark changes; and (ii) the drift-follow signal survives bid–ask costs with positive expected value over ≥500 in-play events, OR the liquidity-gated blender beats a fixed 50/50 market/model blend on Brier score by ≥0.002.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.08266v1", "title": "What Went Wrong with Data Lakes? A 15-Year Reality Check from the Field", "normalized_lane": "data_infra", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Adopt a quarterly swamp-indicator dashboard over GSE's feature store / signal inventory: per-table owner, metadata completeness (target >=90%), 90-day dormancy flags, full source lineage, duplication <20%; trajectory over quarters (not thresholds) is the metric, and deteriorating quarters trigger the stage-based intervention actions.", "gate": "ADOPT the dashboard + quarterly GDAM iff: (a) all six indicators are computable (no missing-instrumentation gaps) within one quarter; (b) metadata completeness ≥90% and duplication <20% at first full run; (c) quarterly re-run takes <2 hours of operator time.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.08578v1", "title": "Lost in the Non-convex Loss Landscape: How to Fine-tune the Large Time Series Model? (SFF)", "normalized_lane": "timeseries_foundation", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Make SFF the default fine-tuning initializer for every sports-TSFM fine-tune (Chronos, Moirai, Lag-Llama, TimesFM): Theta_3 = alpha Theta_1* + (1-alpha) Theta_2 with alpha from {0.5, 0.7} selected on the season-before-test; always run standard full-FT alongside and log the delta to build GSE's internal evidence base.", "gate": "ADOPT SFF as the default fine-tuning initializer if it beats standard full-FT on MSE in the majority of test seasons with no CRPS regression >1%; keep it as an option (not default) if results are mixed; REJECT as default if it underperforms standard FT in 2+ seasons.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.08587v1", "title": "Improving Sharpness in Neural Network Parametric Post-processing", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Train GSE's probabilistic post-processor for game totals (and discrete props) with CRPSmod instead of pure CRPS: Gaussian-family loss with an interval-width penalty (alpha tuned 0.001-0.02 on 2024 walk-forward) to produce sharper central intervals at matched coverage, guarded by a live coverage monitor that rolls back alpha if realized coverage drops >1 point below nominal.", "gate": "ADOPT CRPSmod training if on 2025 frozen test the central-90% interval narrows by ≥5% vs. pure-CRPS training, empirical coverage stays within ±0.5pp of nominal, and mean CRPS does not regress (paired test p<0.05 for width, non-inferiority for CRPS).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.09276", "title": "ERBench: A Benchmark and Testsuite for Equation Discovery Algorithms", "normalized_lane": "symreg_equation_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Make the ERBench 200-formula panel the mandatory regression test for GSE's symbolic-regression pipeline: run the sports-config PySR on all 200 formulas, score Symbolic Recovery/JI/TED plus failure-boundary diagnostic sweeps (recovery vs complexity, noise 0-5%, sample size, domain); no SR config ships to the engine without beating the previous Recovery/JI — and build a SportsEq dev set (~100 known sports formulas: Elo, Glicko-2, TrueSkill, Pythagorean, Kelly, Dixon-Coles).", "gate": "ADAPT if: GSE's current sports-config PySR scores Recovery < 0.40 on the 200-formula panel AND the diagnostic sweeps identify at least one concrete failure axis that a ledger 2166–2172 upgrade is designed to fix.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.09912v1", "title": "Mix, Don't Pick: Why Synthetic Corpus Composition Matters for Time Series Foundation Model Pretraining", "normalized_lane": "timeseries_foundation", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt the MixedSports recipe for all sports-TSFM pretraining: build sports generator families (score-dynamic with key numbers, possession/pacing, usage random walks, injury-shock regime shifts, volatility regimes, market-line generators with known inefficiencies), run matched-budget sweeps (1M windows per family), and train on the equal-weight mixture + real data, then add adversarial generator mining on the mixture's residual errors.", "gate": "ADOPT the MixedSports recipe for all sports-TSFM pretraining if the mixture matches/beats the best single generator on the held-out-season sweep AND real+synthetic beats real-only.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.11120", "title": "Monte Carlo Pass Search: Using Trajectory Generation for 3D Counterfactual Pass Evaluation in Football", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build gse_counterfactual_decision_eval.py: train a discrete-token autoregressive world model on NGS tracking (k-means motion vocabularies, 8->24 token rollouts) plus a possession-value head; for each QB throw/fourth-down decision sample execution-noise and global variants, roll out to the next meaningful interaction, score delta-PV, and report S_mean/S_pct per decision per player plus VaR/CVaR tail-risk summaries of the delta-PV distribution for fantasy sit/start.", "gate": "world-model minADE20 must beat constant-velocity by ≥ 30%; decision-eval pilot on 200 labeled fourth-down decisions must show S_pct separating known-good from known-bad calls (rank correlation with EPA outcome ≥ 0.4).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.13033v3", "title": "Selective Mask Propagation for Multi-Object Tracking", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt the margin-dispatched orchestration pattern for GSE's broadcast-footage tracking lane: base tracker (ByteTrack) every frame, expensive modules (VOS mask propagation, jersey OCR) firing only on margin-signal windows, with the asymmetric override rule (expensive output overrides the base only when confident AND contradicting), plus NFL GTA (pose-guided jersey OCR + team classification).", "gate": "ADAPT the dispatch + gated-correction design if, on the NFL annotation set, adding margin-dispatched VOS improves AssA by ≥ 3.0 points over the base tracker with the same detections, and false-positive SWAPs stay below 10% of SWAP windows.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.13221v2", "title": "From Uncertain Judgments to Calibrated Rankings: Conformal Elo Estimation for LLM Evaluation", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Fit GSE's BT/Elo team ratings with margin-calibrated soft targets: temperature beta via MLE mapping point-margin to win probability sigma(beta*m), soft target y-tilde = sigma(beta**m) per game instead of 0/1 (fixes the stretched ruler where ratings over-react to close wins), and wrap weekly power ratings in split-conformal 90% intervals with regime-dependent (Mondrian) temperatures and quantiles.", "gate": "Adopt if soft-target BT reduces held-out-season Elo-vs-market MAE by ≥ 10% relative (averaged over the 10 leave-one-season-out folds) with Δρ ≥ −0.01, AND conformal intervals achieve empirical coverage within [85%, 95%] at 90% nominal with median width ≤ 80% of the hard-target variant's width.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.16356v1", "title": "Simulation-Augmented Multi-Step Split Conformal Prediction for Aggregated Forecasts", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt simulation-augmented multi-step split conformal for GSE's season-total markets (win totals, season yards/TDs): expanding-window game-level residual collection, center horizon-wise residuals, block bootstrap (b=4 weeks) of 10,000 remaining-season paths, aggregate to 90/95% intervals, then combine with conformal PID online adaptation of quantile levels as the season progresses.", "gate": "ADOPT SA-MSCP for season-total intervals if, on the 2023–2024 holdout, empirical coverage of realised win totals is ≥80% at nominal 90% AND mean interval width is no more than 1.5x the naive baseline width.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.17345v1", "title": "Counterfactual Optimization of Baseball Pitch Sequences and Estimation of Its Impact on Season-Level Statistics", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Port the micro-counterfactual to macro-stat bridge to NFL 4th downs: train a drive-outcome/WP model on pre-play state + decision, swap each historical 4th-down decision counterfactually holding context fixed, aggregate per-coach mean gaps, and regress coach season EPA-per-drive on the gap as a coach decision-quality metric; then run the multi-objective Pareto (WP, EPA, coverage risk) version for game-plan cards.", "gate": "ADAPT the framework if, on the nflverse 4th-down test: (a) the per-coach optimal-vs-actual output gap correlates with season EPA/drive at |r| ≥ 0.5 on the held-out 2025 window, and (b) the estimated Δwin upper bound is stable across two adjacent held-out windows (2024, 2025).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.18686v1", "title": "ForecastBench-Sim: A Simulated-World Forecasting Benchmark", "normalized_lane": "mixed", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a simulated-world calibration benchmark: freeze halftime game states, pose engine questions (final margin, total, 2H points), resolve by Monte-Carlo rollout of a drive-level game simulator (1,000+ sims), score Brier/CRPS against sim-resolved outcomes, run interventional mutations (QB injury, weather shift) to test counterfactual calibration, and generate adversarial tail states (4th-quarter 1-score games, extreme weather) where the bankroll lives or dies.", "gate": "ADOPT sim-resolved calibration if engine calibration curves against sim-resolved outcomes match real-outcome calibration within ±0.05 slope on 2024.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.19642", "title": "Rigorous uncertainty quantification of probabilistic AI weather forecasts with conformal prediction", "normalized_lane": "weather", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Add weather/conformal.py: sequential conformal corrections (Eq. 2-4, alpha=0.1/0.2, eta=0.01, trailing-365-day calibration window) wrapping the ANET2 probabilistic forecast's quantile output per stadium x lead time x variable, layered after the LGBM bias correction (bias fix first, conformal spread second); later add separate upper/lower corrections for extremes (top-5% wind/precip games) since 95th-percentile events still undercover.", "gate": "ADOPT if, within 30 days of simulated burn-in, empirical coverage at 90% lands within ±0.02 of nominal for temperature and wind across ≥ 25/30 stadiums, with CRPS no worse than raw.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.23448v1", "title": "Selective Time Series Forecasting via Metalearning", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a CatBoost meta-regressor predicting each pick's error percentile from pre-game structural descriptors (spread/total movement stats, rest, injury count, back-to-back flag, line sharpness proxy); withhold from posting when predicted error percentile >= q (calibrated to a target posting coverage, e.g. 80%), and validate the zero-shot/adapted protocol NFL->NBA/MLB with 30% target-league adaptation.", "gate": "ADOPT if held-out meta-level ρ ≥ 0.4 and kept-pick hit rate at 80% coverage improves ≥1.5 pp over keep-all with the metamodel beating the interval-width baseline.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.24171v1", "title": "Predicting the 2026 FIFA World Cup with Sufficient Dimension Reduction of Elo Rating Histories", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace GSE's single current-rating-difference feature in the game-outcome head with 2 SIR/SAVE SDR scores from K=6 lagged weekly rating differences (whitened, 3-class slices cover/no-cover/over-under), and run the 2x2 cover x over/under slice design so the second SAVE direction becomes a high-variance-game-script (weather, backup QB) totals feature.", "gate": "ADAPT if the SDR-score model reduces mean log-loss vs the current-difference baseline by ≥0.005 on the 2025 test window with the same feature budget (no extra raw inputs).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.26497v1", "title": "Learning Probabilistic Filters with Strictly Proper Scoring Rules", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Train an energy-score (beta=1) neural ensemble filter as GSE's live probabilistic game-state updater (score/timeouts/field-position dynamics), benchmarked against bootstrap particle and ensemble Kalman filters, serving with N<=100 ensemble members at inference; test on a misspecified simulator with an online recalibration head to measure the real-world robustness gap.", "gate": "ADAPT into a GSE game-state module if the energy-score-trained NN filter matches the particle filter within 5% energy-score on simulated NFL game-state trajectories with N≤100 at inference time.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.27274v2", "title": "BetXplain: An Explanation-Annotated Dataset for Detecting Manipulative Betting Advertisements on Social Media", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Deploy a compliance filter on GSE's affiliate promo copy, sportsbook ad creatives, and sponsored content: sample 500-1,000 promos, triple-annotate with the paper's 3-class taxonomy (Cohen's kappa reported), fine-tune ELECTRA (5 epochs, AdamW, lr 2e-5, inverse-frequency weighted CE) to flag manipulative/deceptive patterns for human review before publication.", "gate": "Adopt if macro-F1 ≥ 0.65 on triple-annotated held-out promos with annotator κ ≥ 0.6 AND deceptive-class F1 ≥ 0.60 (the paper's 0.511 is the bar to clear).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.29203", "title": "Bayesian Best-Arm Identification with Abstention: A Polynomial-to-Exponential Phase Transition", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Evaluate engine versions with inverse-gap-weighted allocation (PGWS): allocate backtest/paper-trade weeks p_i proportional to 1/gap^2 across the production engine + challenger configs, and gate shipping on the Bayesian abstention rule — keep the incumbent iff R_T < r-hat_{T,alpha}, with an adaptive abstention budget alpha_t tied to the cost of a bad ship vs the cost of another evaluation week.", "gate": "ADAPT the allocation rule iff inverse-gap weighting reaches the same ship-decision confidence with ≥20% fewer evaluation weeks than equal-split on historical version comparisons.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2606.29823v1", "title": "Experience Graphs: The Data Foundation for Self-Improving Agents (Trellis)", "normalized_lane": "llm_agents_ai_scientist", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the GSE experience graph (Postgres/SQLite) as the discovery loop's substrate: nodes attempt/artifact/reward/comparison/reflection with derived_from/supersedes edges; query-based access ('what was the frontier last night?' answered <2 min), crash recovery from the frontier query (<5 min, zero duplicate backtests), and a weekly automated experience-mining job flagging bad implementations (sibling underperformance), dead lanes, and recurring failure reflections.", "gate": "ADOPT as the loop's substrate if: analyst query-time test passes (<2 min), crash recovery <5 min with zero duplicate backtests over 3 induced crashes, replay fidelity 5/5, and storage stays <10 GB after 30 nights.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INVENT", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2607.00164v1", "title": "Verifiable Rewards for Calibrated Probabilistic Forecasting", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace/augment GSE's Platt/isotonic probability calibration with calibration against an empirical-rate teacher: bucket historical pick outcomes by (model prob decile, days-to-kickoff, spread bin, league) with hierarchical empirical-Bayes backoff (M=25 pseudocounts), fit the calibrator to minimize squared error vs teacher rates p-hat(x) rather than binary outcomes (removing Bernoulli noise), then distill toward a learned gradient-boosted rate model that adds line movement.", "gate": "ADAPT if calibrator (b) reduces test-window ECE by ≥20% relative vs (a) with Brier no worse than (a) within 0.002.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2607.04389v1", "title": "Ledger 0796 — Decentralized Aggregation of LLM Predictions via Wagering Mechanisms (WALLA)", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Give GSE's ensemble per-game learned weights via WALLA's advantage-aligned rule: train one small MLP per signal source on pre-game features (injury flags, line movement, weather, rest) to predict w_i^* = ((s_i - b_{-i})/2c_3)^+ (per-game Brier advantage vs the leave-one-out pool), aggregate with linear pooling p-hat = sum w_i p_i / W, and test a decision-weighted advantage target A_i^dec = u*(s_i - b_{-i}) with u = realized CLV or Kelly fraction.", "gate": "Season-2 backtest: advantage-aligned aggregation must beat equal-weight aggregation by ≥ 1.5% Brier score and achieve D-Regret ≤ 30% of the equal-weight gap to oracle before production. DM test at 5%.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2607.04590v1", "title": "Attention Limited Reward Learning", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add a cycle-consistency diagnostic to GSE's pairwise rating machinery: build dense comparison graphs (engine-variant pairwise win rates across backtest weeks, or multiple power-rating sources), compute the Hodge decomposition of the empirical log-odds field, report cyclic energy share vs a parametric bootstrap null; when the diagnostic fires, fit regime-conditioned BT r_i(x) = theta_i + phi_i^T x instead of scalar ratings.", "gate": "ADAPT the diagnostic into the model-evaluation pipeline if: (a) on engine-variant comparison data the cyclic energy share exceeds the bootstrap null at p<0.05, OR (b) even under the null, the one-eighth-law misfit price is material (>0.01 bits/comparison).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2607.06166", "title": "When Do Prophets Profit in Prediction Markets?", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Implement Brier proper-bet sizing for GSE's daily card: stake w proportional to (p_GSE - q_market) clipped by a liquidity proxy (expected line-move per dollar from book-count/depth data) instead of flat or Kelly; log per-pick realized CLV decomposed into score gap (accuracy), divergence (disagreement payoff), and liquidity cost as the sizing feedback loop; extend to multi-book shopping with a fourth shopping-bonus term.", "gate": "ADAPT is confirmed if, on the 2024-season backtest, proper-Brier staking beats both flat staking and Kelly on realized ROI with statistical significance (paired bootstrap, 5%) and the three-term decomposition attributes ≥60% of the gain to the score-gap term.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2607.06495v1", "title": "Pitwall: Faithful Natural-Language Race-Strategy Briefings from a Calibrated Real-Time Monte Carlo Engine", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Impose Pitwall's three-part discipline on the GSE engine: (1) bound-constrained parameter set with documented physical bounds and a gating rule — every component gets its own full recalibration on the training window and is evaluated only on the held-out window with its own parameters, optimizing J = rho_Spearman - 2*Brier - ECE, with parity gating (golden-hash regression on a fixed fixture) behind feature flags; (2) CRN counterfactuals for in-play hedge/cash-out decisions under shared random seeds with bootstrap CIs; (3) a typed claim verifier that extracts claims from drafted X posts and rejects any draft contradicted by the engine state snapshot.", "gate": "Accept into the calibration lane if: (1) the bound-constrained parameter set is defined and documented; (2) at least one engine change is gated with the full recalibrate-both-configs protocol and the decision recorded; (3) the X-post claim verifier covers ≥90% of extractable claims per post with 0 contradicted claims published.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2607.08199", "title": "Volatility in Prediction Markets: A Structural Approach", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Add a DR-AS structural volatility forecaster over GSE's odds data (de-vigged consensus p_t, hours-to-kickoff tau_t, cross-book spread s_t as the adverse-selection proxy, book-move-count volume proxy V_t) whose predicted remaining-move scale drives CLV confidence, bet-size scaling, and abstention.", "gate": "ADOPT the structural forecaster if, on the 2025 NFL holdout, DR-AS improves on the GARCH(1,1) baseline by >=15% in volume-weighted interval score with the paired-bootstrap difference significant at 5%. REJECT (keep GARCH or constant vol) if the gain is <10% or insignificant — then cross-book spread is not a sufficient adverse-selection proxy in bookmaker (non-CLOB) markets.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2607.09505v1", "title": "Objective and subjective entropy measures of portfolio suboptimality", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Rank GSE's staking rules (quarter-Kelly, half-Kelly, variance-budgeted Kelly) by the Kelly-gap 1/2||theta - alpha sigma^T pi*||^2 on the Neon picks history, so divergence between realized log-wealth ranking and Kelly-gap ranking isolates estimation error from structural strategy shortfall.", "gate": "Simulated GBM (theta=0.4, sigma=0.2, T=1, 100k paths): for alpha=0.5, the analytic gap 1/2(1-alpha)^2||theta||^2 must match the Monte Carlo mean log-wealth ratio within +-2 standard errors before applying the Kelly-gap ranking to GSE's staking-rule horse race.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2607.11432v1", "title": "Generalizing Preference-based Reinforcement Learning: a Rationality Model for Incomparability", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add a multi-objective pick-selection layer that fits an MOBT softmax over GSE's posted-vs-skipped and abstained pick pairs to recover Garrett's implicit weights over edge, cover probability, and variance, replacing the scalar pick-score ranking with a Pareto-frontier filter.", "gate": "ADOPT the multi-objective selection layer if on 2025 H1 the MOBT model achieves >=0.05 nats/comparison better test log-likelihood than the scalar BT baseline AND the Pareto-frontier filter on 2025 H2 yields posted-pick CLV >= the scalar-ranking baseline's CLV with no worse cover rate. REJECT if the incomparability labels are uninformative (MOBT ~= BT log-likelihood) or the comparison dataset has <500 usable pairs.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2607.11548v1", "title": "Training-Free Off-Screen Player Imputation for Broadcast-Based Spatial Football Analytics", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Implement role-anchored centroid-voting imputation (the paper's B4 training-free baseline) as the front end for any GSE broadcast-video tracking lane, benchmarked against the ignore policy on decision-relevant NFL metrics (pre-snap box-count estimate, receiver separation at throw) rather than trajectory fidelity.", "gate": "Adopt B4 (or a better learned variant) into the GSE tracking pipeline if it cuts the decision-relevant NFL metric error to <=50% of the ignore policy on the held-out weeks; reject broadcast-video tracking for that metric (stick to play-by-play sources) if B4 fails to beat the ignore policy.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2607.12248v2", "title": "When Directional Accuracy Lies: A Base-Rate-Honest Benchmark for LoRA-Adapted TimesFM on Equity Forecasting", "normalized_lane": "timeseries_foundation", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Make the base-rate honesty harness (excess accuracy vs always-favorite/always-home/always-under plus closing-line baselines, McNemar/DM tests with BH-FDR, frozen versioned artifacts) mandatory for every GSE model evaluation so no model ships on raw hit-rate alone.", "gate": "ADOPT the honesty harness as mandatory for all future GSE model evaluations if it successfully reproduces the paper's base-rate demonstration on the sanity dataset AND flags >=1 currently-believed GSE edge as a base-rate artifact on re-scoring; any model whose only evidence is raw hit-rate without base-rate comparison is automatically REJECTED from live consideration.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2607.14430v1", "title": "Prices, Probabilities, and Parlays: Systematic Bias in Sports Prediction Markets", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Apply a time-to-expiry-conditioned (TTE-bucketed power-logit/Platt) calibration map to every GSE market-implied probability before it enters the engine, plus a parlay-specific calibration audit comparing SGP quoted prices against the product of book leg prices.", "gate": "ADAPT the TTE-conditional calibration into GSE's market-implied pipeline if, on one held-out NFL season: (a) the [0,10)-minute bucket gamma-hat differs from the pooled estimate with p<0.05 AND the TTE-conditional map improves log-loss over the pooled map by >=0.005 nats; (b) for parlays, adopt the parlay-specific calibration only if median R deviates from 1.0 by >=2% in the 2-5 leg cells.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2607.15483v1", "title": "Risk-Aware Preference Learning for Stochastic Outcomes", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Fit the Prelec probability-distortion curve w(p)=exp(-(-ln p)^gamma) from GSE engine probabilities to market-implied probabilities per market segment and switch the EV pipeline's edge selector to the CPT-adjusted edge when the fitted gamma sits significantly below 1.", "gate": "ADAPT into the EV pipeline if: (a) fitted gamma < 1 with 95% CI excluding 1 on the training window AND (b) the CPT-adjusted edge selector beats the naive edge selector by >=2pp ROI on the 2024-2025 holdout. REJECT if gamma ~= 1 or the CPT adjustment adds no ROI — the distortion must be measured, never assumed.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2607.15899v1", "title": "ContinuityBench: A Benchmark and Systems Study of Stateful Failover in Multi-Provider LLM Routing", "normalized_lane": "data_infra", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Build a HandoffBench for the GSE agent-bus that plants 2-3 factual anchors in every parent-to-subagent task and measures the Handoff Preservation Rate of returned reports with a calibrated LLM judge, turning anchor loss into a standing reliability metric.", "gate": "ADAPT if: (a) the continuitybench harness reproduces the treatment-vs-baseline CPR gap (treatment >=95%, baseline <=5%); (b) the retry-storm repro shows fixed-interval retries destabilizing and jittered backoff stabilizing; (c) judge calibration on 20 hand-labeled handoff cases reaches >=90% agreement. Adopt HPR as a standing gate only if a pilot shows >=1 anchor-loss event the parent would otherwise not have caught.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2607.17525v1", "title": "FailureAtlas: A Taxonomy of Failure Modes in Multi-Provider LLM Serving Infrastructure", "normalized_lane": "data_infra", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Run the paper's 5x2 failure-mode grid as a reliability audit over every hop between GSE code and its model/API providers (OmniRoute routes, odds polling, agent-bus messaging), classifying each hop and fixing the found defects as scheduled ops hardening rather than research.", "gate": "ADAPT if: (a) all three released reproduction scripts reproduce their claimed failure mechanisms on the lab VM (shared-state turn loss; synchronized-retry saturation vs jitter success; index=0 emission), and (b) the grid classifies every surveyed issue example without forcing. This is infrastructure hygiene, not a prediction edge — schedule as ops hardening.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2607.17991", "title": "Optimal Market Making in Prediction Markets", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Fit the sigma(t,x)=sigma_0+sigma_1(t/T)^eta+sigma_2/(1+x^2) volatility spec to GSE's in-game win-probability paths per sport and add the exposure-skew rule plus the terminal settlement penalty to pick-slate selection so published confidence flattens against directional exposure hardest at coin-flip prices.", "gate": "Adapt the volatility specification and the skew/penalty rules if sigma(t,x) beats constant-volatility on GSE's win-probability paths (AIC) — these are cheap, model-free wins. Do not implement the full HJB quoter unless GSE actually operates a quoting book.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2607.18009v1", "title": "Bayesian Conway-Maxwell-Poisson model with spike-and-slab priors for dispersed count data with application to football scores", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Port the CMP spike-and-slab model to NFL team points (starting from the released repo code, adding Dixon-Coles score-dependence and exponential recency weighting) as a challenger to GSE v5.2.7's totals predictions, replacing full MCMC with a Laplace/VI approximation for production.", "gate": "ADOPT into the GSE totals pipeline if CMP-SAS beats the Poisson-Maher baseline on out-of-sample IGN for totals in >=2 of 3 seasons AND identifies >=3 teams/season with P(Z_i=1)>0.5 (dispersion heterogeneity exists in NFL scoring); REJECT if no team crosses the 0.5 threshold in any season or IGN gains vanish.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2607.18084v2", "title": "WorldCupArena: Fine-Grained Evaluation of Language Models and Deep-Research Agents on Football Forecasting", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt the Scoreline partial-credit metric (45 points for the correct outcome class plus margin/total closeness terms) together with availability-aware aggregation and the lock-before-deadline/score-after verification protocol as GSE's internal engine-evaluation and public-pick verification machinery.", "gate": "The gate for GSE: the Scoreline metric must change model-variant rankings vs raw accuracy on GSE's own data (reproducing the paper's RQ1), or it is decorative. Do not adopt the display calibration (eq. 3) for external reporting — report raw scores.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
